1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,200
The rain hadn't stopped for three days.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,600
She stood at the window, watching the street.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,000
Every car that passed slowed down near the corner.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,400
"You're late," she said without turning around.

5
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,800
I closed the door quietly behind me.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,200
"The bridge was closed. I had to walk."

7
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,600
She finally looked at me, and I knew.

8
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,000
Something had changed while I was gone.

9
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,400
"They came looking for you this morning."

10
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,800
"Two men. They didn't leave a name."

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,200
I sat down slowly and lit a cigarette.

12
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,600
"What did you tell them?"

13
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:32,000
"Nothing. I said I didn't know you."

14
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,400
That was a lie, and we both knew it.

15
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,800
"You should have never come back here."

16
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,200
The clock on the wall ticked too loudly.

17
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,600
"I came back because of the letter."

18
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:44,000
Her face went pale at the word.

19
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,400
"There is no letter. Do you understand?"

20
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,800
"Whatever you think you read, forget it."

21
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,200
Outside, a car door slammed shut.

22
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,600
We both froze and listened to the silence.

23
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,000
"They're here," she whispered.

24
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,400
I reached for the light and turned it off.

25
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,800
Footsteps climbed the stairs, one by one.

26
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,200
"Whatever happens, don't say my name."

27
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:05,600
The handle turned. The door held.

28
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,000
And then, for a long moment, nothing.
